I want to present another opinion on that suggestion.

The problem is that you put something into your BoH that shouldn't go
there. If you put, by accident, a wand of cancellation into your BoH,
or put, by accident, a sack which contains a wand of cancellation into
your BoH, it's the same; your BoH and all contained gear will be lost.

So you should employ other methods to avoid that accident.

Some people recommend to name the sack DANGER (or something like that).
But what's the difference between naming the sack DANGER and naming the
wand DANGER; really not that much. So I think that is also not a good
recommendation.

Other folks propose to leave the dangerous wand (and spare BoHs and bag
of tricks) at your stash, and completely avoid to carry those dangerous
items around. IMO, this is a better suggestion.

What turned out to work in my case were two provisions. First, I play (on
NAO) with colouring; assigning bright colours to those dangerous items
makes them immediately visible when you're handling the inventory. Second,
I assign those wands standard letters in the inventory; the first wand of
cancellation is 'c', the next 'd'. So I see them on top of the list, and
even if playing fast I know (or feel) that typing, say, 'c' will always
have to be checked. Those two combination fixed the problem for me. And I
carry them (together with all my other masses of loot) always around with
me.

